# Quality Review Checklist

Full scored report: `evals/QUALITY_EVALUATION_REPORT.md`. Use when touching untrusted I/O, on-disk cells, compaction, or CI.

## P0 — prefer fix when editing

- [ ] Unexpected `catch(...)` on receive/send: log (`SWC_LOG_CURRENT_EXCEPTION`) — do not add new empty catches (R-P0-3)
- [ ] `SerializedClient` connect: honor caller `timeout` (today ignored) (R-P0-4)
- [ ] Do not remove existing `header_len` / `swc.comm.payload.max` receive guards

## P1 — data integrity when editing ranger / CellStore / CommitLog

- [ ] Truncated/corrupt cell decode: must fail-fast (`err = SERIALIZATION_INPUT_OVERRUN`); do not log-and-continue with partial cells (R-P1-1)
- [ ] CellStore `blks_count` / `idx_size_*`: sanity-cap against schema/RAM
- [ ] Compaction `Blocks::apply_new`: avoid CS-live + old-log-remain window if `commitlog.remove` fails after `cellstores.replace`
- [ ] Do **not** “fix” insistent FS Interface sync retries — intentional outage resilience

## CI / tests (when changing workflows or claiming coverage)

- [ ] Remember: CI runs only with `[TEST COMMIT]`; default matrix does **not** run `TEST=2` integration
- [ ] Prefer unit tests under `tests/libswcdb*`; extend integration only for cluster behavior
- [ ] Null-check `m_metrics` on `ev->error` paths if touching AppContext error handling

